soak-test-census: core=4 threads=7 C0 C1 W1 C2 W2 C3 W3
soak-test-census: this is the boot-time lottery and NOT where the run settles: a rendezvous wake queues the peer on the waker's own core (DECISIONS 138, how a saturated workload is made to hand threads across cores), so each group converges onto one core within a few exchanges
soak-test-census: the beat line's drifted= is how many responders, callers and grinders are no longer on the core the census above put them on; while it reads 0 that census is current, and a nonzero one is followed by the census that replaces it
soak-test-census: tick waiters are excluded from drifted= because their movement is the point rather than a surprise, and it is already crossings= (design/roadmap/0221-a-soak-that-crosses-cores.md)
